# TEMPLATE — copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
#
#     cp .env.example .env        (Git Bash)
#     Copy-Item .env.example .env (PowerShell)
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this template is committed. Never put a real email
# address or API key in this file.

# REQUIRED. The SEC requires a descriptive User-Agent identifying who is making
# the request. Requests without one get blocked outright. Format is "Name email".
# edgartools reads this variable automatically.
EDGAR_IDENTITY="Your Name your.name@example.com"

# DO NOT PUT AN API KEY IN THIS FILE, OR IN `.env`.
#
# Not a style rule. `_bootstrap` loads `.env` on every import, so a key here is
# AMBIENT: present in every run whether or not that run wants it. That is exactly
# how one nearly got spent. On 2026-09-02, with the default `claude_code` backend
# selected, `ClaudeCodeBackend` handed the CLI subprocess the parent environment
# with no filtering — and the Claude Code CLI treats ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as an
# authentication method. So the calls would very likely have billed the key while
# every facts record stamped `backend: claude_code` and every printed dollar was
# labelled "notional". The claim would have been false and the spend real.
#
# Two guards now exist, and neither replaces keeping the key out of here:
#   - `seat_only_env()` strips every API credential from the CLI's environment
#     (tests/unit/test_seat_billing.py), so `backend = "claude_code"` means what
#     it says on any machine, including one that does have a key.
#   - every record carries `billing: "seat" | "api_key"` and
#     `credentials_withheld`, so "these dollars are notional" is a fact on the
#     record rather than an inference from the config.
#
# THE `api` BACKEND IS STILL FULLY SUPPORTED — it is just OPT-IN now. Extraction
# measured about half the cost through the API, and a single stage can be moved
# across without touching the others (see PER-STAGE OVERRIDES in config/llm.toml).
# To use it, put the key in `.env.api`, which nothing loads automatically, and
# supply it for that invocation only:
#
#   $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = (Select-String .env.api `
#       -Pattern '^ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=(.+)$').Matches[0].Groups[1].Value
#   # then set [llm] backend = "api", or [llm.<stage>] backend = "api"
#
# Every `.env*` is gitignored except this template.

# OPTIONAL. edgartools' own cache location. Leave unset — this project manages
# its own cache in companies/<TICKER>/data/raw/ so a company's cached filings sit
# beside its config and deliverables rather than hidden in a home directory.
# EDGAR_LOCAL_DATA_DIR=""
